# >>> jig secret-ignore >>>
# jig secret-prevention floor (ADR-0013) — git-ignore common secret
# files so they can't be staged by accident. Edit above/below the
# markers; this block is regenerated by jig and re-runs are idempotent.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
!.env.dist
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
credentials/
.jig/semantic-index-claude-hook.json
.jig/semantic-index-codex-hook.json
.jig/semantic-index-events.jsonl
.jig/servo-hint-shown
# <<< jig secret-ignore <<<

# >>> jig runtime state (do not track) >>>
# jig runtime state (bug 028) — per-checkout telemetry, queues, and
# spec/decision markers jig writes each session. Tracking them churns
# every commit; per-checkout markers also collide at merge. Edit
# above/below the markers; regenerated by jig, re-runs are idempotent.
# Already tracking these? Untrack without deleting: git rm --cached <path>
.claude/skill-usage.jsonl
.claude/context-growth-read-events.jsonl
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json
.jig/spec-ref
.jig/decision-scratch/
.jig/decision-suppressions.log
# <<< jig runtime state <<<

# Node / npm (spike deps now; the eventual runtime package later)
node_modules/

# Build output — generated by `npm run build` (esbuild, spec 004-02). Regenerated
# from adapters/eds/ + core/ + connectors/ into the testbed's served tree; not
# source, don't track.
probes/eds-testbed/scripts/airlock/

# Rig artifacts — screenshots / captures generated by the rigs (e.g. rig:uc1's
# no-flicker challenger screenshot, spec 005-01). Regenerated on each run; the
# human-review copy is attached to the slice, not tracked as source.
rig/out/
